@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# DM05 base: experimental ApxInf-native fixed-profile implementation
+
+**PUBLIC post-measurement documentation, not new execution evidence.** Runtime
+source bytes in this delta retain the job329543 hashes recorded in the source
+manifest. This document supersedes the earlier build-time notes but was not
+executed, rebuilt, patch-applied or reviewed as a correctness gate.
+
+## Scope and ownership
+
+The `dm05` family has independent `weights.rs`, `model.rs`, `model_runner.rs`,
+`backend.rs` and `load.rs` modules. It does not import another model-family
+directory. The existing native `ModelRunner` binding and Python `Dm05Policy`
+connect author CPU input/output transforms to Rust/CUDA model computation.
+No Torch model, Torch graph or external inference engine is the native model.
+
+Supported measured tuple: A800-SXM4-80GB SM80, CUDA12.8 build target, BF16,
+batch1, three448x448 images, no history, unpadded prefix882or876, ten Euler
+steps, horizon50,32internal and14public actions. Source rejects padded/history
+profiles and prefix lengths above974. Other hardware/profiles are not accepted
+by this result. GPU driver version was not recorded in job329543 evidence;
+do not substitute a driver from an older build or another allocation.
+
+The model owns SigLIP27, 2x2 pooling and Gemma3 projection; Gemma3 prefix34 with
+four plus-one RMS norms, QK norm before half-split RoPE and image-block masks;
+and action34 with time AdaRMS, branch post-norms, BF16 gates and full10step flow.
+The safe CUDA facade supplies GEMM, FA2, normalization and tensor operations.
+Missing rounded rotary/pool/FP32-bias/score-rounding operations were added in
+this isolated backend snapshot, not to the author's implementation.
+
+Weights and packing have loaded-model lifetime. Schedule-derived modulation
+tensors are computed natively once and retained. Prepared inputs, masks,
+prefix KV, latent state and graph arena have owning runtime lifetime. Request
+values are copied into stable buffers; model computation and segment handoff
+remain on GPU until explicit public output download. Public preprocessing,
+token/state construction and action reconstruction are CPU policy work, not
+CPU model layers. Independent transfer tracing and lifetime tests were not run.
+
+## Author arithmetic and public wrapper boundaries
+
+The author's warmed suffix graph has BF16 Linear and persistent BF16 state;
+its first eager suffix uses FP32 action projection/Euler helpers. Job329543
+used the warmed BF16 branch, matching author329331's two captured profiles and
+zero disabled profiles. `APXINF_DM05_EAGER_MATH=1` selects an unmeasured alternate
+source path, not another result from this campaign.
+
+Native public inputs are canonical CPU patch rows, token IDs, action mask and
+provided noise. Formal fixture storage encodes token IDs below262208 exactly
+as F32 because the existing fixture reader lacks I32; the driver decodes u32
+and the runtime still uploads native I32. No precision threshold was changed.
+The policy uses the author's CPU resize/tokenization/normalization and final
+absolute-action transforms. It does not construct the author's Torch model.
+
+Native noise was the author's saved exact BF16 tensor, including upload in
+native timing. The author timing includes CUDA RNG generation. This boundary
+difference must accompany the nominal full-policy latency ratio. Neither
+canonical-CPU-to-normalized-CPU timing nor policy wall time is pure graph replay.
+
+## Actual formal result, not release acceptance
+
+Author source: dexmal/opendm `03f799120d425ead51d9482bb1da950b6dabade9`.
+Checkpoint: Dexmal/DM05 base `5cd18734814abb075a9ccfd9ad6d16777b5cf10e`.
+Reference job329331; native/public job329543 COMPLETED0:0 in2m25s.
+
+Forty full-policy samples: author median277.657942ms/mean277.5912135ms/
+p95278.9247174ms; native median149.352156ms/mean149.3726382ms/
+p95150.10012425ms. Nominal median ratio1.85908225x, with the noise/RNG caveat.
+Native canonical CPU input to normalized CPU output median139.0278145ms;
+it is not directly scope-compatible with author's267.1750877ms GPU-inner value.
