+# DM05 portable source adapters (PUBLIC, post-measurement, NOT RUN)
+
+These adapters were curated after job329543. They are not its private task
+scripts, have not been executed/rebuilt/imported during packaging, and must not
+be relabelled as measured script bytes. The Rust benchmark, runtime, binding and
+policy source hashes remain the measured ones. No environments, asset data,
+raw inputs/actions, binaries, archives or submission scripts are distributed.
+
+## External prerequisites
+
+The source delta requires the separately supplied archived private Hy foundation,
+including its uncommitted content. It is not a clean7f37642/self-contained build.
+Obtain the official source/checkpoint under their own terms; retain all licenses
+and notices. Callers supply compatible Rust/CUDA/Python/native build dependencies
+and the optional official OpenDM CPU transform dependencies. This helper set
+does not install dependencies, download assets, reserve devices or submit jobs.
+
+Use explicit caller-owned locations represented by these environment variables:
+
+```bash
+export APXINF_ROOT="${PATCHED_SOURCE_ROOT:?}"
+export CARGO_TARGET_DIR="${OWNED_BUILD_OUTPUT:?}"
+export CUDA_HOME="${CUDA_TOOLKIT_ROOT:?}"
+export PYO3_PYTHON="${COMPATIBLE_PYTHON_INTERPRETER:?}"
+export APXINF_CUDA_ARCH=sm_80
+export CHECKPOINT="${DM05_BASE_CHECKPOINT:?}"
+export REFERENCE="${COMPLETED_OFFICIAL_RESULT_DIRECTORY:?}"
+export INPUTS="${NEW_OWNED_FORMAL_INPUT_DIRECTORY:?}"
+export CORE_OUTPUT="${NEW_OWNED_CORE_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY:?}"
+export POLICY_OUTPUT="${NEW_OWNED_POLICY_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY:?}"
+export OPENDM_ROOT="${OFFICIAL_SOURCE_ROOT:?}"
+```
+
+The completed reference must provide the four named case directories, prepared
+CPU tensors, exact BF16 initial noise, complete public actions and root metadata.
+These artifacts are private external inputs, not included examples. Do not
+regenerate noise and call it the recorded reference. Inspect actual suffix graph
+status: the measured reference used hot BF16 graph arithmetic, not eager FP32.
+
+## CPU-only serialization and build-only commands
+
+The new input directory must not already contain case subdirectories.
+
+```bash
+HELPERS="$APXINF_ROOT/python/apxinf/examples/dm05_experimental"
+"$PYO3_PYTHON" "$HELPERS/prepare_inputs.py" --reference "$REFERENCE" --output "$INPUTS"
+bash "$HELPERS/build_native.sh"
+```
+
+The serializer performs CPU layout/dtype conversion of saved tensors only. The
+build helper compiles/links but does not import the extension, execute the
+benchmark, run tests or submit jobs. Configure an already available native
+module search directory explicitly after building; no environment is bundled.
+
+## Actual inference commands require separate authority and allocation
+
+**This source handoff authorizes no additional GPU work.** If independently
+authorized later, run model commands only within an allocated GPU step. The
+native driver and public benchmark enforce allocation environment markers.
+Use default warmed BF16 math; do not set `APXINF_DM05_EAGER_MATH` for reproducing
+the recorded branch.
+
+```bash
+export PYTHONPATH="${NATIVE_MODULE_DIRECTORY:?}:$APXINF_ROOT/python/apxinf:$OPENDM_ROOT${PYTHONPATH:+:$PYTHONPATH}"
+"$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/examples/dm05_benchmark" "$CHECKPOINT" "$INPUTS" "$CORE_OUTPUT"
+"$PYO3_PYTHON" "$HELPERS/decode_core.py" --reference "$REFERENCE" --native "$CORE_OUTPUT" --checkpoint "$CHECKPOINT"
+"$PYO3_PYTHON" "$HELPERS/benchmark_policy.py" --reference "$REFERENCE" --checkpoint "$CHECKPOINT" --source "$OPENDM_ROOT" --output "$POLICY_OUTPUT"
+```
+
+CPU decode uses official public normalization/action reconstruction, not model
+inference. It requires the official source/dependencies visible on the Python
+search path. Inputs are three images plus public state/prompt; the measured
+model has no history or padded-prefix support. Output is complete50x14 absolute
+CPU actions; internal model width is32. The native core boundary includes
+canonical CPU upload/download and must not be called pure graph latency.
+
+## Saved-output arithmetic only
+
+These commands construct no model and require no GPU allocation:
+
+```bash
+"$PYO3_PYTHON" "$HELPERS/compare_saved.py" --reference "$REFERENCE" --core "$CORE_OUTPUT" --public "$POLICY_OUTPUT" --output "${ARITHMETIC_REPORT:?}"
+"$PYO3_PYTHON" "$HELPERS/summarize_saved.py" --reference "$REFERENCE" --core "$CORE_OUTPUT" --public "$POLICY_OUTPUT" --output "${SUMMARY_REPORT:?}"
+```
+
+No commands above were run during packaging. The actual job329543 evidence is
+summarized separately in the public aggregate result and source manifest. Formal
+output budget is unchanged: relL2<=0.05 and cosine>=0.999. Public timing must
+disclose that native uses saved noise while author timing includes CUDA RNG.
